  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-priority uncertainty is establishing a clean single-modality baseline. config_001 (RNA-only, single profile, PCA-2000) is the simplest, least confounded configuration: it uses a standard linear encoder (PCA), avoids aggregation complexity (single profile), and isolates the RNA signal. This gives a reference accuracy/F1 against which I can later (a) compare the image modality (config_010) to determine which modality carries more discriminative signal, and (b) assess whether multimodal fusion actually adds value over the best single modality. Starting with a minimal baseline maximizes interpretability of every subsequent experiment and prevents attributing multimodal gains to encoder or aggregation choices that are simultaneously being varied."
